-- examples/checks/agg-phrase-data.rofl — WHAT THE PHRASE WORLDS READ (docs/aggregates.md, "The sentence form,
-- as built"), loaded as written: candidates and ballots (c3 has none), scores under keys (two keys share 20),
-- flags, a weighted graph with two ways from a to c, members of two groups and who of them voted, how many
-- votes each candidate needs, two percents, and where a counter starts; and the ranks groups give their members
-- (g1 ranks m1 twice, at 3 and at 1).
